Subject: [PATCH] test: pin testnet compatibility to the v6 kernel VK tree root

The private kernel circuits on v6 differ from the ones the testnet was deployed with: they charge the teardown call's AVM startup gas, require a surviving nullifier link to resolve to a non-revertible note hash, and do not clamp the delayed public mutable time horizon on a scheduled change to the same value. Each changes the kernel circuits and so the VK tree root v6 builds.

diff --git a/yarn-project/aztec/src/testnet_compatibility.test.ts b/yarn-project/aztec/src/testnet_compatibility.test.ts
index ecdee7d4db2b5c08293b8302a024738ea38b5db8..a12a6e286d548ea609f9a9a2ab23501c04fb5d85 100644
--- a/yarn-project/aztec/src/testnet_compatibility.test.ts
+++ b/yarn-project/aztec/src/testnet_compatibility.test.ts
@@ -11,7 +11,7 @@ import { computeExpectedGenesisRoot } from './cli/cmds/standby.js';
  */
 describe('Testnet compatibility', () => {
   it('has expected VK tree root', () => {
-    const expectedRoots = [Fr.fromHexString('0x2d89003cc2dc62b06f07d83d3635c66c63fc43668369d30e7ee516f908ee10e3')];
+    const expectedRoots = [Fr.fromHexString('0x1032cbb2f61a9c1151370ebc35c8ea20d1a726e3388eb94e84291c2b2fecb5d3')];
     expect(expectedRoots).toContainEqual(getVKTreeRoot());
   });
